Subject: Recognize a leading package name in interface resource entries

Applies to: RCR rosidl_runtime_py 0.15.2-3.rcr.2,
rosidl_runtime_py/get_interfaces.py.

Observed failure: get_interfaces reports builtin_interfaces/Time as a grid_map_msgs
message. Its resource index contains grid_map_msgs/msg/GridMap.idl alongside
transitive dependency entries. The existing own-package filter recognizes only
/package/ in the middle of a path, so it fails when package/ starts the path.

Rationale and scope: normalize a leading owning-package segment before the
existing filter. Preserve ordinary relative and embedded-package paths, API
behavior and dependency filtering. No package-specific names or path inventory.

Verification: all nine original SDK targets pass (51 behavioral cases and four
linter cases), with no skips. resource_paths_test passes all three path-position
subcases (one unittest case). The extracted product has a separate consumer gate.

Upstream: the selected published implementation retains this boundary case,
inspected 2026-11-23. No matching upstream association is recorded.
https://bazel.ros.org/modules/rosidl_runtime_py/0.15.2-3.rcr.2/source.json

